From f967ffed516f59010cfb09c38d2f8e6c56a79de4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LLCOOLT <114613597+LLCOOLT@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:15:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 36/36] gx: shutdown releases the objects initialize made

The empty texture's bind group, texture, view and sampler and the pipeline
layout were left to the program's exit, released after Dawn's device was
gone: on OpenGL ES (Linux handhelds) the exit crashed in BindGroupLayout's
destructor. aurora_shutdown now lets go of them with the rest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 lib/gx/gx.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/gx/gx.cpp b/lib/gx/gx.cpp
index 3d4e62b..4373709 100644
--- a/lib/gx/gx.cpp
+++ b/lib/gx/gx.cpp
@@ -681,6 +681,13 @@ void initialize() noexcept {
 
 void shutdown() noexcept {
   // TODO we should probably store this all in g_state.gx instead
+  // (every object made at initialize: one left to the program's exit is released after Dawn's device, which
+  // crashed the exit on OpenGL ES)
+  g_emptyTextureBindGroup = {};
+  sPipelineLayout = {};
+  sEmptyTextureView = {};
+  sEmptyTexture = {};
+  sEmptySampler = {};
   sTextureBindGroupLayout = {};
   for (auto& item : g_gxState.textures) {
     item.ref.reset();
-- 
